# mcp_tools — vendored MCP server + tools

The MCP server injected into the OSWorld guest VM for the hybrid (GUI + MCP)
action space. This is the tool set behind the paper's headline numbers.

```
mcp/
  mcp_server/
    server.py            # FastMCP server
    launch_server.sh
    tools/
      package/           # executable tool implementations (calc, impress, writer, code, chrome, vlc, os)
      apis/              # tool JSON schemas (mirror of ../tools/tools_registry.json)
  osworld_mcp_client.py  # client injected into the VM
```

## How it's used

`MCP_SRC_ROOT` (default `./mcp_tools`, see `configs/env.example.sh`) points here;
`OSWorld-main/desktop_env/desktop_env.py::_inject_mcp_files` copies
`mcp/mcp_server/` and `mcp/osworld_mcp_client.py` into the guest at boot. Set
`MCP_SRC_ROOT=0` to fall back to a stock OSWorld-MCP checkout instead.

